\name{ConfirmAIDesignSemantics}
\alias{ConfirmAIDesignSemantics}
\title{Confirm Batch/Condition/Subject Column Semantics for AI-Guided Integration}
\usage{
ConfirmAIDesignSemantics(object, design)
}
\arguments{
  \item{object}{A \code{SingleCellExperiment} object.}
  \item{design}{A named list mapping experimental-design roles to
    \code{colData} column names. At minimum a \code{batch} role must be
    present; additional roles may include \code{condition}, \code{subject}
    and \code{sample}.}
}
\value{
  \code{object} with a \code{ai_design_confirmation} state record
  attached. The record stores the role-to-column mapping,
  (1) the \emph{object-skeleton fingerprint} (n_cells, n_features,
  colData column names, presence of rowData), (2) a value-level signature
  for each \code{design} column, (3) the ledger fingerprint before the
  confirmation was written (as returned by
  \code{\link{GetAnalysisLedger}}) and (4) the timestamp at which
  confirmation happened. The confirmation becomes stale (is rejected by
  the \code{run_integration} prerequisites) when any of the following
  happens: any design column referred to in \code{design} is removed or
  renamed, its values are replaced/renamed (the same column name but with
  different cell-level label assignments, e.g. the batch labels
  \code{a}/\code{b} are re-mapped to \code{T_cell}/\code{B_cell} under
  the same column name), or the skeleton changes. This is deliberately
  more conservative than the raw \code{GetAnalysisLedger} fingerprint:
  reductions, analyses or other analysis-state writes that do not touch
  the design columns or the object skeleton \emph{do not} invalidate the
  confirmation.
}
\description{
  Explicitly records that the caller (a human user or a trusted upstream
  routine) has verified which columns of \code{colData(object)} carry the
  technical batch, biological condition, subject and sample identifiers.
  This is the \emph{only} way to open the design-semantics gate checked by
  the \code{run_integration} AI action; a plan cannot self-declare that
  design has been confirmed.
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
  sce <- ConfirmAIDesignSemantics(
